From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omarchy Ferrix <maintainers@omarchy.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] exynos-modem: keep NV sinks and crash records in a private
 directory

The root daemon created and truncated the fixed names
/tmp/rfs-nv_{normal,protected,user}.bin and wrote
/tmp/modem_crash_<ts>.json, following symlinks. Anyone who can write to
/tmp could point those writes at another file.

Move both into /run/exynos-modem (scratch.rs):

- Each path component is opened with openat(O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW) from
  the previous directory's fd. Ancestors must be owned by root (or the
  daemon's user) and not be group- or other-writable. The directory must
  be owned by the daemon's user with mode 0700. It is created when
  missing; an existing one with another owner or mode is refused, not
  repaired.
- NV sinks are opened with openat(O_CREAT|O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK) and are
  truncated only after fstat shows a regular file we own, with one link
  and no group/other bits. A symlink, hard link, FIFO, directory, or
  foreign file is refused untouched. The RFS exchange still completes
  and the data is dropped, as upstream did when the open failed.
- Crash records use O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW.

NV reads still come only from the read-only factory mounts. Both kernel
backends are otherwise unchanged. --print-config prints scratch_dir.
---
 crates/exynos-modem/src/boot/s5300.rs |  17 +-
 crates/exynos-modem/src/main.rs       |   2 +
 crates/exynos-modem/src/rfs.rs        | 133 +++++--
 crates/exynos-modem/src/scratch.rs    | 497 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 623 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/exynos-modem/src/scratch.rs

